{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790313802,"nonce":"vxx4UZ5FbSp+SI275kFULqP+r1c=","title":"Lua debug: getlocal and setlocal on another thread give nothing","message":"debug.getlocal(co, level, n) and debug.setlocal(co, level, n, v) on a suspended coroutine give nothing, where lua5.4 reads and writes the coroutine's frame. Found by the L-debug-library verifier; same result on both tiers.\n\n    local co = coroutine.create(function(a) local b = a * 2; coroutine.yield(); print(\"after\", b) end)\n    coroutine.resume(co, 3)\n    print(debug.getlocal(co, 1, 1))\n    print(debug.getlocal(co, 1, 2))\n    print(debug.setlocal(co, 1, 2, 10))\n    coroutine.resume(co)\n\nlua5.4: 'a 3', 'b 6', 'b', 'after 10'. zylua (tiered and ZYLUA_LLVM=1): nil, nil, nil, 'after 6'.\n\nA coroutine's frames need their call-site spills kept per thread so the other thread's getlocal can read them and setlocal can mark them for read-back on resume.","files":null}]}